WEBVTT

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.650
In accordance with Master Neshinbara's wishes,

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:13.030
in three minutes we shall enter gravitational navigation

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.110
and leave this airspace.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.080
As such, I request that those fighting on Musashi's behalf

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.660
survive the battlefield until then. Over.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:22.790
Huh?

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:23.580
Let's go!

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.170
Hey, where are we going?

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.210
Just follow me!

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.760
Eh?! But where are we going?

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:26.750
Locked on!

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.710
That's the rumored—

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.470
Sniper Maiden!

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.760
Of all the things to say!

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.430
You may blast away as many of those cisterns as you want

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.890
since we've already paid for them. So take them down!

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.480
Uh, shrine maidens can't shoot people.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:55.070
I'll pave the way, guys!

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.950
Oh, my! I see they severed the transport cables.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.530
Manager, incoming hostiles!

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.960
Track and Field Club, retreat!

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.670
Most impressive. I'll let the baseball team take over.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.920
It's time I entered the fray myself.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.350
Let 'em rip!

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.930
Home run!

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.450
And now to finish them off.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:42.700
Here I go!

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.590
Student Council Secretary Velásquez

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.210
and Supreme Federation Vice Chancellor Hironaka Takakane!

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.130
No way!

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:04.760
They brought their nation's Testament Armament all the way to the border?!

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:08.140
Do you recognize those weapons, Master Neshinbara? Over.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.480
Yeah, they're the Crus Temperantia.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:14.520
My Vetus slows down my opponents' time by half.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.610
"Time is money," after all!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.230
As for my Novum here,

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:23.110
it reduces the amount of times you can use your abilities.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.410
Shit!

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.210
Even if you detract from its skills, it's still a ten-ton pup!

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.710
I'm the Sixth Special Agent, Naomasa!

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.180
The Track and Field captain, Era Fusae!

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:52.600
Pathfinder Byakko is leaving the Tres España flagship.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.640
Come on, Pathfinder Byakko!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:56.310
Go!

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:05.490
She has superior speed and power!

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.910
Damn it!

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.130
Bind, Slicing Dragonfly!

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:28.300
I am the Vice Chancellor of Musashi Ariadust Academy, Honda Futayo!

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:31.760
Much obliged!

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:37.440
I've been rather interested in Musashi's Suzaku!

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.770
There are Four Sacred Gods of War on the level of Divine Weapons,

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.650
one of which is my Byakko.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.740
Could your Suzaku be one as well?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.500
What the...?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.420
My Byakko's ability falls under "pathfinding".

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:08.260
No matter what the situation or location, it can always find footing and dodge

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.760
as easily as if it were standing on a large road.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.930
Now go, Pathfinder Byakko!

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.100
Do not leave the building

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.730
until evacuation orders have been issued.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:25.190
Azuma, did you finish on your end?

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.820
Judge! I just need to run by my room

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.450
and check on Miriam and that girl.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.410
I see you didn't hand her over to the facility.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.240
That was a wise move.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.750
The majority of Musashi's facility sponsors

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.500
are from the Ohiroshiki family.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:44.340
But I think you could have entrusted her with us.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.710
With you?

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.800
Well, with our current technology,

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:51.180
we could bear each other's child without sex,

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.140
but that's probably a different form of excitement all together.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:56.390
Yes?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.850
What is "sex"?

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.940
W-Well, you see...

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:07.650
It means that someone is in a deep, close relationship with another.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:10.450
It has a long history.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:16.330
So for instance, when would you and Naito have sex?

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.330
He has no idea what he's getting into!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.590
Well, uh, maybe after we have a fight?

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.630
Yeah! It lets you kiss and make up overnight.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:30.470
Hmm, this has been most informative!

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:41.690
You see, I can properly bunt any ball that comes my way!

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.360
As long as I'm around, the others will rack up the runs.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.360
That's how I serve as Vice Chancellor!

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:56.830
You are exactly as I thought you would be.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:08.300
Damn you!

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.010
Left shoulder, let out a roar!

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.190
Purge the right leg!

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:39.040
Farewell, Fake Suzaku.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.500
Well done, Naomasa.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:46.540
You owe me for this.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:50.050
Preposterous! They used a God of War to buy time?!

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.020
I'm counting on you, cross-dressing Honda!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:09.730
I, Vice-president Honda Masazumi of Musashi Ariadust Academy,

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.280
suggest a truce!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:16.570
This battle arose from a misunderstanding on Tres España's part.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:18.070
Neither side has anything to gain from this.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:19.990
That's because...

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.290
Okay, everyone,

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:27.420
Masazumi has something amusing to say to you.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.590
Kitano Tenmangu Shrine

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:43.850
S-So, I shall borrow the power of the God of Laughter from the age of the gods.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:50.400
In 16XX, Earth was engulfed in the flames of the apocalypse!

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.690
Hello, I'm Utamaru.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:01.910
Wanna get some grilled meat? Grilled meat!

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.540
Masazumi, if I may, wouldn't it be best

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.830
if you returned to the issue at hand?

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.710
Listen up, everyone!

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.590
The reason this battle continues is because—

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:19.930
I am Tachibana Gin.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:23.140
the third Special Agent of Tres España's Alcalá de Henares.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:25.100
En garde!

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.060
Masazumi!

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.190
Get back!

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.650
A sword breaker?!

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.950
If you wish to fight, face me!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.080
I shall take back everything I lost.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.830
Take this!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.330
I got her!

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:51.960
I can't look!

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.680
Arcabuz Cruz!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:04.760
Slicing Dragonfly!

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:07.850
Horizon!

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:10.390
Armament of Deadly Sins, Lypē Katárripsi!

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:14.570
Juana, you're up!

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:17.280
Armament of Deadly Sins, Akidía Katárripsi!

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:20.650
Super-drive.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:31.080
It's heavy! No, isn't this... disgust?

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.830
It is the deadly sin, disgust.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:38.920
The power of disgust will affect whatever aspect of yourself you consider "evil."

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:42.890
I-It's not like my chest size bothers me!

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.640
Wouldn't you agree, Masazumi?

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:48.270
Horizon!

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.890
What should I do...?

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:03.700
Get in position,

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.870
Tres España's baseball team!

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.370
Fire!

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.290
Squish?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.670
Whoops! What a pity!

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.250
This is my "real side".

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.880
I came up to the roof because I like high places,

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.130
but your timing's great!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.050
Could you give me that Armament of Deadly Sins?

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:35.350
Not again!

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.110
Fire!

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:44.660
I managed to get a bunch of Tres España's confidential data.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.700
Nice, Tenzo!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.540
A naked man fell from the sky!

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.660
And there go my secrets of war!

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.000
Worse yet,

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:59.040
the first person I've ever held like a princess is a naked man!

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.010
Horizon!

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:03.760
Ah, that dirty whore.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.590
How was my expression?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:07.760
Just shoot already!

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.180
Judge.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:20.860
Your broom got me in the balls!

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:22.610
Who cares?! Here we go!

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:26.740
Lypē Katárripsi.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.220
E-Everyone, atta—

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:55.270
It's time!

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.520
Everyone on deck, head to the center of the ship!

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.270
We are entering gravitational navigation. Over.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.110
Arcabuz Cruz!

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:06.280
Bind!

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.210
Honda Futayo...

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.960
No, I want to go outside!

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.300
You can't! It is dangerous outside right now.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.130
You should listen to your Mama!

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:29.680
No!

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:30.970
Stop it, you two!
No!

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.430
Let's calm down and have sex!

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.430
Now hurry up and have sex!

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.440
Azuma...?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.360
You need to have sex!

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:45.150
Wh-Where in the world did you learn about that?

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:49.740
A girl I know just taught me all about sex.

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.990
A-And here we were acting like we're a faux family...

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:54.200
Mama...?

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.290
To think someone seduced our Daddy.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.080
This is truly a trap-like development.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:03.250
Our family is like a trap in and of itself.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:07.010
I-I'm sorry, Miriam!

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.670
I understand that I am in the wrong,

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.180
so let's just hurry and have sex!

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:16.520
Horizon!

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.810
I order you to get dressed.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.360
It would be horrible if your stomach got cold.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.320
I don't get why you needed to punch me though.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.570
Judge, it was within the allowable margin of error for issuing a warning.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:29.990
Horizon!?

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.740
Horizon, you're not a woman to be trifled with.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.030
Most impressive!

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.700
What?! Why are you acting like you're a commander?

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.200
And seriously, get dressed! Also...

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:42.250
Fine, I'll be a good boy and stay.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:45.040
Hey, Seijun! What's with the naked rope routine?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.250
Shut up!

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:49.130
Don't move until the ship stops. You're getting in the way.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:50.090
My bad!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:54.010
Mitotsudaira, could you use your silver chains to transport Horizon to Musashi?

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:56.010
I'm afraid they won't reach.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:58.140
Once we've left gravitational navigation,

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:01.850
let's use the transport cables to land this cargo ship in Okutama.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.610
We'll be in England soon...

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:13.070
That's—

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:17.080
The ship shall hereby enter coasting mode.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:19.700
We are headed straight for England. Over.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.660
Our ship, Musashi,

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.210
shall hereby enter England's waters.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:29.170
We will do as England's control ship asks and go around back. Over.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:37.430
This is the British Convoy, Granuaile.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:39.770
I am its captain, Grace O'Malley.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:42.680
I am warning you as one of the Fairy Queen's Trumps.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:46.230
My ship orders yours to come to an immediate halt!

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:51.490
Your ship's relationship with Tres España and the Testament Union is unclear.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:55.360
Furthermore, England is not affiliated with the Far East!

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:58.120
If you do not stop immediately,

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.870
England will use force to make you stop.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.790
Four assailants have boarded

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:10.000
They are identified as members of Oxford Academy's Student Council,

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.260
Supreme Federation, and Trumps.

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.930
We'll be right on top of England in three minutes.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:20.180
Neshinbara, don't tell me...

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.890
Judge. I'm headed over!

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:25.810
We win if they fail to stop Musashi within three minutes!

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.230
Herrlich!

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:36.280
England is fighting them?

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:42.200
Has the upcoming Spanish Armada made them anxious of their standing with the Testament Union? Well?

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.160
How was that?

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:46.370
They're unscathed!

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:48.630
I am one of the ten Trumps,

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:53.380
Vice Chancellor Robert Dudley of Oxford Academy.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.220
I am one of the ten.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:59.390
I am Vice-President William Cecil!

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:02.890
I never expected the head of the humanities clubs,

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:06.730
the athletic poet Ben Jonson, to come here!

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:09.810
You see, the Trumps were my idea.

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:11.900
So I want to associate with them as much as possible.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:14.690
That is why today my favorite pupil is here...

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.110
The most popular author in England right now.

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:21.870
I never would have imagined she was Shakespeare.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:25.620
Gems are meant to be kept tucked away in a box.

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:26.500
Isn't that right?

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:30.210
I need to be careful not to become the underdog.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.670
Wh-What's this?

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.920
Wouldn't you be a beaten dog if you lost? Well?

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:37.130
Here I go!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:47.980
May God be with you!

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.360
Are you "sharing" your weight with us?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.730
The wealthy should give to the poor.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.150
Keep it to yourself!

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.370
Deflecting Testament Signs?

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:09.580
You're supposed to "fend off hardships".

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:14.170
This is one of England's Testament Armaments,

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.760
the large gauntlet Brachium Justitia Vetus!

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.260
My Brachium Justitia Vetus' crushing power

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:27.310
is the ability to control weapons on the battlefield from a distance.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:30.440
R-Right now, you are my hostages!

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.770
Ah, a dance to warm the water,

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.730
regardless of its restrained heart.

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.320
What do you think?

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:44.030
How do you like the lines an athletic poet reads to the spirits?

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:45.330
Naruze!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:46.620
I'm fine.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:49.870
I won't die before Asama finishes firing.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.920
This isn't the time for that!

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.580
Fan fictions are great.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:54.960
Why don't you write one?

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:57.710
It can even be a short story.

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:59.670
You should make it equivalent to other works.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:01.760
It can even count as your club activity.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:03.800
Care to join the club?

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:05.680
There's a lot you could learn.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.350
Wouldn't it be a nice break from all those shrine offerings?

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.640
I know.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.770
How about you make the title, "What I Want To Do"?

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.520
I see you're done chatting.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.230
I'm going to give our demands.

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:24.700
Allow Musashi to fall under England's complete and total control.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:27.370
Or are you going to abandon your friends?

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.080
Hey, now! Don't underestimate us.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:30.870
Wh-Why are you naked?

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.540
Listen, no matter what's going on in the world,

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.420
I'd never abandon a friend.

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.960
And Naruze there is a pretty gutsy gal!

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.380
What are you going to do?!

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.300
F-Fire!

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:59.480
2nd Special Agent, Kiyonari Urquiaga, hath arrived!

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:02.900
I warmly welcome you, Heretic!

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:05.820
Oh, words of praise!

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.950
O Wind, come before her as she stands

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.080
and pass through like a vestige!

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:15.000
You defeated Professor Galileo. Wasn't your name Noriki?

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.830
You don't have to say it if you already know.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:19.750
I see...

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:22.260
So that assault was a diversion

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:25.300
so you could rescue the witch and deliver a fighter.

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:27.010
I'm not a fighter.

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:28.760
I'm a laborer.

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:30.600
Two minutes left!

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:32.850
Please pull through until then.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.070
Cecil!

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.780
Okay!

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:48.280
An extremely heavy projectile has penetrated to Level Four.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:49.410
I perceive this attack as dangerous. Over.

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:52.790
Goodness, there is nothing for you to do here.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:54.910
Kimi, aren't you going to do something?

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.960
I'm just a normal student.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.290
Although that's true of Noriki as well.

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:03.340
And as a priestess, you can't help either, can you?

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:05.090
Being a priestess has its disadvantages, huh?

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.510
Sure does! After all, you can't shoot people.

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.050
I-I think you have the wrong idea about me.

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:15.480
Aren't there other things you could do instead?

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:17.350
But...

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:24.940
What a vibrant scream.

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:28.740
Didn't you notice that I have been supporting my own boobs?

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:31.240
Of-Of course I didn't notice!

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:32.740
Now for round two!

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:36.040
Ouch!

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:40.960
Wh-Wh-Wh-What is that round thing?!

00:22:40.960 --> 00:22:43.840
Wh-What just fell on me?

00:22:44.670 --> 00:22:46.090
Here goes three at once!

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:49.090
"The arrows were picked up by the wind and fell onto the ground."

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:54.310
Sorry to keep everyone waiting.

00:22:55.430 --> 00:22:56.390
Sorry I'm late.

00:22:58.180 --> 00:23:01.980
I am Musashi Ariadust Academy's Secretary, Toussaint Neshinbara.

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:08.780
"He ran as if he weighed nothing, swiftly approaching his foes."

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:13.490
This is my spell, Weighted Words.

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:16.870
Shakespeare, be careful! He's an author.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:23.500
"The enemy was suddenly forced to the ground upon standing up."

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:28.510
"The weight of the fall made such an impact that the surrounding area exploded."

00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:35.600
Well, I guess everything worked out okay.

00:23:37.720 --> 00:23:40.140
That is a rather interesting spell.

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:43.230
I suppose I should say I am a fellow writer.

00:23:43.770 --> 00:23:45.270
You don't think that level of writing

00:23:45.270 --> 00:23:48.780
could overthrow another writer, do you?

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:51.740
Now then...

00:24:04.580 --> 00:24:05.790
Let's get started.
